Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 17:00:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] =?UTF-8?q?refactor:=20metar=E2=86=92local=5Fstation,?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20add=20DropNode,=20fix=20ERA5=20batching=20+=20NWP=20date=20c?=
 =?UTF-8?q?lamp?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Rename all metar node/edge references to local_station throughout
  graph_builder, gnn, train, and tests — inductive node type supports
  both airport METAR (Phase 1) and IoT sensors (Phase 2) without retraining
- Add DropNode to CropOSGNN (40% node masking during training) so model
  learns the ERA5-only path and is robust to missing station data at inference
- Add src/preprocessing/labels.py: METAR p01i gauge readings as primary labels,
  ERA5 precipitation as spatial fill everywhere else
- Fix ERA5 ingestion: batch 50 grid points per API call (~40 calls vs 1,980)
  to stay within Open-Meteo free tier rate limits
- Fix NWP ingestion: clamp start date to 2016-01-01 (API minimum), save empty
  DataFrame gracefully if all stations fail instead of crashing on concat
- Add local_station_dropout: 0.4 to configs/model.yaml; train.py reads it
- Fix GitHub Actions download workflow: add pyarrow, set PYTHONPATH
- Fix train.yml trigger: narrow configs path to model.yaml + training.yaml only
- pyproject.toml: add package-mode = false
